1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,999
Three o'clock on a Tuesday afternoon,

2
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,459
on the mountain side of a town on Maui,

3
00:00:03,460 --> 00:00:05,939
an engine crew pulls up to a burning field

4
00:00:05,940 --> 00:00:07,674
and reports what it can see.

5
00:00:07,734 --> 00:00:10,173
A fire about twenty feet by a hundred,

6
00:00:10,174 --> 00:00:11,586
moving toward the ocean.

7
00:00:11,610 --> 00:00:13,309
It is the same field they were called

8
00:00:13,310 --> 00:00:14,590
to that morning.

9
00:00:14,650 --> 00:00:15,649
What nobody standing

10
00:00:15,650 --> 00:00:16,989
in it knows is that the phones

11
00:00:16,990 --> 00:00:21,406
in the town below them stopped working hours ago.

12
00:00:21,466 --> 00:00:23,610
This is a story about a warning.

13
00:00:23,670 --> 00:00:26,650
Not about whether one was sent, because one was.

14
00:00:26,710 --> 00:00:28,129
About what it was sent over,

15
00:00:28,130 --> 00:00:29,969
and what it was sent by,

16
00:00:29,970 --> 00:00:32,911
and which of the two the state had actually built.

17
00:00:32,954 --> 00:00:34,753
Over the next half hour you will hear what

18
00:00:34,754 --> 00:00:36,433
the largest warning system of its kind

19
00:00:36,434 --> 00:00:38,514
in the world was actually for,

20
00:00:38,574 --> 00:00:40,113
what happened in the town on the morning

21
00:00:40,114 --> 00:00:42,393
before the fire that everyone remembers,

22
00:00:42,394 --> 00:00:43,033
why the message

23
00:00:43,034 --> 00:00:45,333
that went out went out at sixteen minutes past

24
00:00:45,334 --> 00:00:48,013
four, and what the state's own investigators wrote

25
00:00:48,014 --> 00:00:50,575
at the end of five hundred and eighteen pages.

26
00:00:50,576 --> 00:00:53,370
A warning system is not the equipment you own.

27
00:00:53,430 --> 00:00:55,149
It is the thing you are in the habit

28
00:00:55,150 --> 00:00:57,724
of using.

29
00:00:57,784 --> 00:01:00,143
Hawaiʻi has more outdoor warning sirens

30
00:01:00,144 --> 00:01:02,018
than any other place on earth.

31
00:01:02,078 --> 00:01:04,686
That is not a boast made by an outsider.

32
00:01:04,746 --> 00:01:05,765
It is the first line

33
00:01:05,766 --> 00:01:08,887
of the state's own description of the system.

34
00:01:08,947 --> 00:01:11,746
"Hawaiʻi has the largest single integrated Outdoor

35
00:01:11,747 --> 00:01:13,726
Siren Warning System for Public Safety

36
00:01:13,727 --> 00:01:14,899
in the world."

37
00:01:14,959 --> 00:01:16,998
More than four hundred of them stand

38
00:01:16,999 --> 00:01:18,078
on the islands.

39
00:01:18,138 --> 00:01:20,328
About eighty of those are on Maui.

40
00:01:20,388 --> 00:01:21,835
They are tested.

41
00:01:21,895 --> 00:01:24,483
Not occasionally, and not after an incident.

42
00:01:24,517 --> 00:01:27,157
On a schedule, in public, in daylight,

43
00:01:27,217 --> 00:01:29,296
on the first business day of every month,

44
00:01:29,297 --> 00:01:31,356
together with the emergency broadcast system

45
00:01:31,357 --> 00:01:34,324
and the local radio and television stations.

46
00:01:34,384 --> 00:01:36,164
Which means that for decades,

47
00:01:36,224 --> 00:01:37,704
on one morning a month,

48
00:01:37,764 --> 00:01:39,983
everybody on those islands has heard exactly what

49
00:01:39,984 --> 00:01:41,590
that system sounds like.

50
00:01:41,650 --> 00:01:44,119
And the state publishes what it is for.

51
00:01:44,179 --> 00:01:46,044
The list is not short.

52
00:01:46,104 --> 00:01:47,319
Tsunamis.

53
00:01:47,379 --> 00:01:48,687
Hurricanes.

54
00:01:48,747 --> 00:01:50,148
Dam breaches.

55
00:01:50,208 --> 00:01:51,330
Flooding.

56
00:01:51,390 --> 00:01:52,837
Wildfires.

57
00:01:52,897 --> 00:01:54,670
Volcanic eruptions.

58
00:01:54,730 --> 00:01:56,131
Terrorist threats.

59
00:01:56,191 --> 00:01:58,149
Hazardous material incidents.

60
00:01:58,209 --> 00:01:59,796
Wildfires are on the list.

61
00:01:59,856 --> 00:02:01,915
They are on the list in the state's own words,

62
00:02:01,916 --> 00:02:04,095
published on the state's own page,

63
00:02:04,096 --> 00:02:06,598
before any of this happened.

64
00:02:06,658 --> 00:02:08,817
There is one more thing on that page,

65
00:02:08,818 --> 00:02:11,542
and it is the part almost nobody knows.

66
00:02:11,602 --> 00:02:14,071
The sirens do not tell you what to do.

67
00:02:14,131 --> 00:02:15,904
They are not a message.

68
00:02:15,964 --> 00:02:17,743
They are an instruction to go and find

69
00:02:17,744 --> 00:02:18,851
the message.

70
00:02:18,911 --> 00:02:20,910
The state's own guidance is that if you hear

71
00:02:20,911 --> 00:02:22,730
a siren tone at any time other

72
00:02:22,731 --> 00:02:24,651
than a scheduled test,

73
00:02:24,711 --> 00:02:26,791
you should tune in to local radio,

74
00:02:26,851 --> 00:02:29,330
television or cable for emergency information

75
00:02:29,331 --> 00:02:31,876
and instructions from the authorities.

76
00:02:31,936 --> 00:02:33,848
That is the whole design.

77
00:02:33,908 --> 00:02:35,527
A sound that reaches everybody,

78
00:02:35,528 --> 00:02:38,095
followed by a message that explains it.

79
00:02:38,155 --> 00:02:39,096
Hold on to that,

80
00:02:39,135 --> 00:02:40,794
because the second half of it is going

81
00:02:40,795 --> 00:02:42,541
to matter more than the first.

82
00:02:42,542 --> 00:02:44,175
Now the week before.

83
00:02:44,235 --> 00:02:46,874
On the first of August, twenty twenty-three,

84
00:02:46,875 --> 00:02:48,674
the National Weather Service issued

85
00:02:48,675 --> 00:02:50,354
a forecast discussion

86
00:02:50,355 --> 00:02:52,334
that predicted stronger trade winds

87
00:02:52,335 --> 00:02:54,554
and dry air arriving with the passage

88
00:02:54,555 --> 00:02:57,314
of a hurricane, and mentioned the possibility

89
00:02:57,315 --> 00:02:59,154
of Red Flag conditions by early

90
00:02:59,155 --> 00:03:00,357
the following week.

91
00:03:00,417 --> 00:03:01,976
A Red Flag Warning is a statement

92
00:03:01,977 --> 00:03:04,256
that the weather itself is now capable of turning

93
00:03:04,257 --> 00:03:06,176
a small ignition into a fire

94
00:03:06,177 --> 00:03:07,669
that cannot be caught.

95
00:03:07,729 --> 00:03:09,188
The hurricane was called Dora,

96
00:03:09,189 --> 00:03:11,591
and it never came near the islands.

97
00:03:11,651 --> 00:03:14,458
It passed about five hundred miles to the south.

98
00:03:14,459 --> 00:03:16,278
What it did was pull.

99
00:03:16,338 --> 00:03:17,977
The gap between its low pressure

100
00:03:17,978 --> 00:03:20,057
and the high pressure to the north squeezed

101
00:03:20,058 --> 00:03:21,877
the air between them, and the wind

102
00:03:21,878 --> 00:03:23,898
that came out of that gap was dry,

103
00:03:23,958 --> 00:03:25,739
and it came down the mountains.

104
00:03:25,740 --> 00:03:27,220
On the third of August,

105
00:03:27,280 --> 00:03:29,619
the forecast discussion specifically mentioned

106
00:03:29,620 --> 00:03:30,539
the possibility

107
00:03:30,540 --> 00:03:32,519
of severe fire weather developing early

108
00:03:32,520 --> 00:03:33,921
in the coming week.

109
00:03:33,981 --> 00:03:34,960
That same period,

110
00:03:34,961 --> 00:03:38,621
a forecaster contacted his fire contacts directly,

111
00:03:38,681 --> 00:03:40,541
telling them to expect strong,

112
00:03:40,601 --> 00:03:43,021
dry winds on the Monday and Tuesday,

113
00:03:43,081 --> 00:03:43,760
and warning them

114
00:03:43,761 --> 00:03:45,600
that a Fire Weather Watch would be issued

115
00:03:45,601 --> 00:03:46,853
over the weekend.

116
00:03:46,913 --> 00:03:49,332
And the report records something about that call

117
00:03:49,333 --> 00:03:51,565
that is worth saying slowly.

118
00:03:51,625 --> 00:03:53,844
The forecaster recognised that this much notice

119
00:03:53,845 --> 00:03:55,766
of such a warning was rare.

120
00:03:55,826 --> 00:03:57,005
On the fifth of August,

121
00:03:57,006 --> 00:03:58,705
the service raised its level of concern

122
00:03:58,706 --> 00:04:00,205
and predicted that Monday

123
00:04:00,206 --> 00:04:02,705
and Tuesday would bring critical fire weather,

124
00:04:02,706 --> 00:04:05,029
with Tuesday especially dry.

125
00:04:05,089 --> 00:04:08,609
At thirty-three minutes past three in the morning
on the sixth of August,

126
00:04:08,669 --> 00:04:10,028
Red Flag Warnings were issued

127
00:04:10,029 --> 00:04:12,992
for the leeward portions of the Hawaiian Islands.

128
00:04:13,052 --> 00:04:14,917
Lahaina was named in them.

129
00:04:14,977 --> 00:04:16,076
On the fourth of August,

130
00:04:16,077 --> 00:04:18,236
the forecast office in Honolulu sent a notice

131
00:04:18,237 --> 00:04:19,697
to state agencies,

132
00:04:19,757 --> 00:04:22,636
including the state's emergency management agency,

133
00:04:22,637 --> 00:04:23,676
about high winds

134
00:04:23,677 --> 00:04:26,037
and impending critical fire weather.

135
00:04:26,097 --> 00:04:27,756
And early on the eighth of August,

136
00:04:27,757 --> 00:04:30,396
between three in the morning and half past nine,

137
00:04:30,397 --> 00:04:31,856
the service repeated its wind

138
00:04:31,857 --> 00:04:34,396
and Red Flag warnings and predicted gusts

139
00:04:34,397 --> 00:04:36,414
of up to sixty miles an hour.

140
00:04:36,474 --> 00:04:38,386
So the forecast was right.

141
00:04:38,446 --> 00:04:39,708
It was early.

142
00:04:39,768 --> 00:04:41,494
And it named the place.

143
00:04:41,554 --> 00:04:43,473
Which raises an obvious question,

144
00:04:43,474 --> 00:04:45,986
and the state's own investigators answered it.

145
00:04:45,987 --> 00:04:47,766
Their sixth finding is that there is little

146
00:04:47,767 --> 00:04:48,826
perceptible difference

147
00:04:48,827 --> 00:04:51,126
between Hawaiʻi's Red Flag criteria

148
00:04:51,127 --> 00:04:53,297
and a typical summer day,

149
00:04:53,357 --> 00:04:55,486
and that this may have contributed to how

150
00:04:55,487 --> 00:04:57,419
the forecast was received.

151
00:04:57,479 --> 00:05:00,038
In a place where the trade winds blow most

152
00:05:00,039 --> 00:05:02,738
of the year and the leeward side is dry most

153
00:05:02,739 --> 00:05:03,799
of the year,

154
00:05:03,859 --> 00:05:06,238
the warning that says today is dangerous looks

155
00:05:06,239 --> 00:05:07,578
a great deal like the page

156
00:05:07,579 --> 00:05:09,608
that says today is Tuesday.

157
00:05:09,668 --> 00:05:11,727
And their eighth finding is about where

158
00:05:11,728 --> 00:05:13,298
the numbers came from.

159
00:05:13,358 --> 00:05:14,517
The fire weather forecasts

160
00:05:14,518 --> 00:05:16,217
and the Red Flag Warnings were based

161
00:05:16,218 --> 00:05:18,637
on data collected at the airport in Honolulu,

162
00:05:18,638 --> 00:05:20,610
which is on a different island.

163
00:05:20,670 --> 00:05:22,809
West Maui did not have the automated weather

164
00:05:22,810 --> 00:05:23,329
stations

165
00:05:23,330 --> 00:05:25,609
that would have shown where Red Flag conditions

166
00:05:25,610 --> 00:05:27,783
actually existed on the ground.

167
00:05:27,843 --> 00:05:29,962
So the warning that arrived was correct,

168
00:05:29,963 --> 00:05:31,022
and it was general,

169
00:05:31,023 --> 00:05:35,063
and it was assembled on another island.

170
00:05:35,123 --> 00:05:36,662
The fires started before dawn,

171
00:05:36,663 --> 00:05:38,474
and there was more than one.

172
00:05:38,534 --> 00:05:40,553
At twenty-two minutes past midnight,

173
00:05:40,554 --> 00:05:42,653
a fire began upcountry, at Olinda,

174
00:05:42,654 --> 00:05:44,625
on the other side of the island.

175
00:05:44,685 --> 00:05:46,968
It grew quickly and it took days.

176
00:05:47,028 --> 00:05:49,387
At thirty-four minutes past six in the morning,

177
00:05:49,388 --> 00:05:51,207
on the mountain side of Lahaina,

178
00:05:51,208 --> 00:05:52,887
a second fire started.

179
00:05:52,947 --> 00:05:53,946
The origin and cause

180
00:05:53,947 --> 00:05:55,847
of that fire are on the record,

181
00:05:55,907 --> 00:05:57,766
they were published by the County of Maui

182
00:05:57,767 --> 00:06:00,827
and the federal Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco,

183
00:06:00,887 --> 00:06:02,467
Firearms and Explosives,

184
00:06:02,527 --> 00:06:04,983
and they are not in dispute in this film.

185
00:06:05,043 --> 00:06:06,563
"At 6:34 a.m.,

186
00:06:06,623 --> 00:06:08,942
the fire originated off Lahainaluna Road

187
00:06:08,943 --> 00:06:11,402
in the unmaintained vegetation near utility pole

188
00:06:11,403 --> 00:06:15,063
25 as a result of molten metallic material —

189
00:06:15,123 --> 00:06:16,263
sparks —

190
00:06:16,323 --> 00:06:18,082
ejected from the re-energization

191
00:06:18,083 --> 00:06:20,283
of broken power lines above."

192
00:06:20,343 --> 00:06:21,744
Broken lines.

193
00:06:21,804 --> 00:06:23,484
Power returning to them.

194
00:06:23,544 --> 00:06:25,263
Metal melting and falling into grass

195
00:06:25,264 --> 00:06:26,895
that had not been cut.

196
00:06:26,955 --> 00:06:28,574
The fire chief said it in one sentence

197
00:06:28,575 --> 00:06:30,015
at the news conference:

198
00:06:30,075 --> 00:06:33,046
the origin and cause of the Lahaina fire is clear.

199
00:06:33,106 --> 00:06:35,482
The classification is Accidental.

200
00:06:35,542 --> 00:06:38,986
Not incendiary, not natural, and not undetermined.

201
00:06:39,046 --> 00:06:40,186
That is the answer,

202
00:06:40,246 --> 00:06:43,045
it was published in October of twenty twenty-four,

203
00:06:43,046 --> 00:06:45,429
and this film will not be raising it again.

204
00:06:45,430 --> 00:06:48,529
But something else had already happened
that morning, before the fire,

205
00:06:48,530 --> 00:06:51,336
and it decided more than people realise.

206
00:06:51,396 --> 00:06:53,675
The wind arrived across central and western Maui

207
00:06:53,676 --> 00:06:55,073
in the early hours.

208
00:06:55,133 --> 00:06:56,813
Trees came down.

209
00:06:56,873 --> 00:06:58,831
Utility poles came down.

210
00:06:58,891 --> 00:07:01,360
Power lines came down across roads.

211
00:07:01,420 --> 00:07:03,759
At twenty minutes to six in the morning —

212
00:07:03,760 --> 00:07:06,240
nearly an hour before the fire started —

213
00:07:06,300 --> 00:07:08,559
the police were logging downed poles and lines

214
00:07:08,560 --> 00:07:09,279
at Keawe Street,

215
00:07:09,280 --> 00:07:12,016
on the northbound lanes of the highway.

216
00:07:12,076 --> 00:07:13,395
That intersection is the one

217
00:07:13,396 --> 00:07:15,275
that carries traffic north and south

218
00:07:15,276 --> 00:07:16,436
through Lahaina,

219
00:07:16,496 --> 00:07:18,864
and it is how you reach the bypass.

220
00:07:18,924 --> 00:07:19,923
The log's own summary

221
00:07:19,924 --> 00:07:22,090
of the effect is four words long.

222
00:07:22,150 --> 00:07:24,851
Limited evacuation from south to north.

223
00:07:24,911 --> 00:07:27,190
Before anything was burning in that town,

224
00:07:27,191 --> 00:07:29,290
one of the ways out of it was already narrower

225
00:07:29,291 --> 00:07:31,467
than it had been the day before.

226
00:07:31,527 --> 00:07:33,146
Two words are going to keep coming up,

227
00:07:33,147 --> 00:07:35,913
and they are the two directions that matter here.

228
00:07:35,914 --> 00:07:37,919
Mauka means toward the mountain.

229
00:07:37,979 --> 00:07:40,123
Makai means toward the sea.

230
00:07:40,183 --> 00:07:42,652
Lahaina sits on a slope between the two.

231
00:07:42,712 --> 00:07:44,299
The fire came mauka.

232
00:07:44,359 --> 00:07:46,058
Everything the town was built to be warned

233
00:07:46,059 --> 00:07:47,618
about came makai.

234
00:07:47,678 --> 00:07:49,197
The morning fire was fought hard,

235
00:07:49,198 --> 00:07:51,697
by ground crews with private bulldozers

236
00:07:51,698 --> 00:07:52,777
and water tankers,

237
00:07:52,778 --> 00:07:55,766
cutting perimeter lines and soaking the ground.

238
00:07:55,826 --> 00:07:58,308
It was contained before nine in the morning.

239
00:07:58,309 --> 00:08:00,549
And then, in the County's own words:

240
00:08:00,609 --> 00:08:02,188
all available indicators showed

241
00:08:02,189 --> 00:08:04,877
the fire was fully contained and extinguished.

242
00:08:04,878 --> 00:08:06,140
No flames.

243
00:08:06,200 --> 00:08:07,369
No smoke.

244
00:08:07,429 --> 00:08:09,888
No perceptibly combusting material observed,

245
00:08:09,889 --> 00:08:11,616
for several hours.

246
00:08:11,676 --> 00:08:13,215
At ten to eight that morning,

247
00:08:13,216 --> 00:08:14,915
the relieving crew walked the burned ground

248
00:08:14,916 --> 00:08:16,142
and looked at it.

249
00:08:16,202 --> 00:08:17,181
The officer noted

250
00:08:17,182 --> 00:08:19,221
that power lines had already come down along

251
00:08:19,222 --> 00:08:20,661
the gulch behind the houses,

252
00:08:20,662 --> 00:08:23,881
and that the lines still standing were swaying

253
00:08:23,882 --> 00:08:24,894
in the wind.

254
00:08:24,954 --> 00:08:26,713
At twenty-seven minutes past eleven,

255
00:08:26,714 --> 00:08:29,234
a third fire started upcountry, at Kula.

256
00:08:29,294 --> 00:08:31,856
It burned uncontained for over a week.

257
00:08:31,916 --> 00:08:33,695
There was a fourth on the island that day

258
00:08:33,696 --> 00:08:34,757
as well.

259
00:08:34,817 --> 00:08:35,876
Emergency responders

260
00:08:35,877 --> 00:08:38,354
on Maui were not managing one fire.

261
00:08:38,414 --> 00:08:39,493
They were managing four,

262
00:08:39,494 --> 00:08:41,613
and continuing to take new calls across

263
00:08:41,614 --> 00:08:42,741
the island.

264
00:08:42,801 --> 00:08:44,280
And then, in the late morning,

265
00:08:44,281 --> 00:08:46,060
the town lost its phones.

266
00:08:46,120 --> 00:08:48,543
The state's timeline puts it plainly.

267
00:08:48,603 --> 00:08:49,582
High winds crippled

268
00:08:49,583 --> 00:08:51,663
the communications infrastructure,

269
00:08:51,723 --> 00:08:54,282
destroying cellular phone communication within

270
00:08:54,283 --> 00:08:56,702
the Lahaina region in the late morning of August

271
00:08:56,703 --> 00:08:57,759
the eighth.

272
00:08:57,819 --> 00:09:00,058
The report then spells out what that meant,

273
00:09:00,059 --> 00:09:02,239
and it is worth hearing all of it.

274
00:09:02,299 --> 00:09:04,439
With no cellular communication,

275
00:09:04,499 --> 00:09:05,978
residents and tourists were not able

276
00:09:05,979 --> 00:09:07,979
to receive emergency alerts,

277
00:09:08,039 --> 00:09:09,438
communicate with loved ones,

278
00:09:09,439 --> 00:09:12,524
or receive incoming or outgoing calls or texts.

279
00:09:12,584 --> 00:09:15,053
Not able to receive emergency alerts.

280
00:09:15,113 --> 00:09:16,512
That is the state's own sentence,

281
00:09:16,513 --> 00:09:17,832
about the late morning,

282
00:09:17,833 --> 00:09:19,765
hours before the town burned.

283
00:09:19,825 --> 00:09:21,598
The police lost them too.

284
00:09:21,658 --> 00:09:24,037
Officers in Lahaina had no cellular capability

285
00:09:24,038 --> 00:09:26,917
at all and worked the entire incident on portable

286
00:09:26,918 --> 00:09:28,539
and vehicle radios.

287
00:09:28,599 --> 00:09:30,998
There were once landlines in houses for exactly

288
00:09:30,999 --> 00:09:32,229
this reason.

289
00:09:32,289 --> 00:09:34,589
Most households no longer have them,

290
00:09:34,649 --> 00:09:36,748
and the report says it does not know

291
00:09:36,749 --> 00:09:37,448
whether the ones

292
00:09:37,449 --> 00:09:39,088
that remained were even working once

293
00:09:39,089 --> 00:09:40,470
the power went out.

294
00:09:40,530 --> 00:09:42,950
At ten to one in the afternoon,

295
00:09:43,010 --> 00:09:44,889
a county entry logged network issues

296
00:09:44,890 --> 00:09:46,750
at Lahaina locations —

297
00:09:46,810 --> 00:09:49,269
the senior centre, the fire station.

298
00:09:49,329 --> 00:09:51,668
At thirteen minutes past one, the shelter

299
00:09:51,669 --> 00:09:54,108
at the Lahaina Recreation Center reported

300
00:09:54,109 --> 00:09:55,885
that it had nobody in it.

301
00:09:55,945 --> 00:09:58,043
Shelter population now zero.

302
00:09:58,103 --> 00:09:58,922
At two o'clock,

303
00:09:58,923 --> 00:10:01,560
the shelter at the Lahaina Civic Center closed.

304
00:10:01,561 --> 00:10:04,441
At seventeen minutes past two in the afternoon,

305
00:10:04,501 --> 00:10:04,880
the crews

306
00:10:04,881 --> 00:10:07,060
on the morning fire reported it extinguished

307
00:10:07,061 --> 00:10:10,592
and returned to quarters.

308
00:10:10,652 --> 00:10:12,146
Thirty-eight minutes.

309
00:10:12,206 --> 00:10:14,405
That is the distance between the crews reporting

310
00:10:14,406 --> 00:10:16,865
the morning fire out and the same ground

311
00:10:16,866 --> 00:10:19,040
being reported on fire again.

312
00:10:19,100 --> 00:10:21,279
Here is how the County described what happened

313
00:10:21,280 --> 00:10:24,030
in between, and this is the whole of it.

314
00:10:24,090 --> 00:10:26,429
Despite diligent monitoring of the fire scene

315
00:10:26,430 --> 00:10:29,430
and deployment of significant resources,

316
00:10:29,490 --> 00:10:30,609
embers from the morning phase

317
00:10:30,610 --> 00:10:33,609
of the fire remained undetected and were rekindled

318
00:10:33,610 --> 00:10:34,889
by a severe wind event

319
00:10:34,890 --> 00:10:38,169
at approximately two fifty-two in the afternoon.

320
00:10:38,229 --> 00:10:39,368
The County has been explicit

321
00:10:39,369 --> 00:10:40,729
about the firefighters,

322
00:10:40,789 --> 00:10:43,717
and it said so at the same news conference.

323
00:10:43,777 --> 00:10:45,276
Its assistant chief said they wanted

324
00:10:45,277 --> 00:10:47,116
to make abundantly clear to the community

325
00:10:47,117 --> 00:10:48,796
that their firefighters went above

326
00:10:48,797 --> 00:10:51,416
and beyond their due diligence to be as confident

327
00:10:51,417 --> 00:10:54,116
as they could be that the fire was completely

328
00:10:54,117 --> 00:10:56,649
extinguished before they left the scene.

329
00:10:56,709 --> 00:10:58,848
And the state's investigators reached the finding

330
00:10:58,849 --> 00:11:01,036
that sits underneath that.

331
00:11:01,096 --> 00:11:02,515
Their sixty-seventh finding

332
00:11:02,516 --> 00:11:04,635
is that the firefighters performed mopup

333
00:11:04,636 --> 00:11:05,855
as proven successful

334
00:11:05,856 --> 00:11:07,615
under typical weather conditions —

335
00:11:07,616 --> 00:11:10,955
and that under the severe conditions of that day,

336
00:11:10,956 --> 00:11:12,675
this level of mopup appears

337
00:11:12,676 --> 00:11:14,525
to have been insufficient.

338
00:11:14,585 --> 00:11:16,804
Mopup is the work of turning over a burned area

339
00:11:16,805 --> 00:11:19,190
and drowning what is still hot in it.

340
00:11:19,250 --> 00:11:21,769
It is a procedure, and it has a standard,

341
00:11:21,770 --> 00:11:24,227
and the standard was the one that works.

342
00:11:24,287 --> 00:11:25,781
That is the finding.

343
00:11:25,841 --> 00:11:28,031
Not that anybody left early.

344
00:11:28,091 --> 00:11:28,830
That the method

345
00:11:28,831 --> 00:11:31,070
that has always been enough was not enough

346
00:11:31,071 --> 00:11:32,464
in that wind.

347
00:11:32,524 --> 00:11:34,323
At five to three in the afternoon,

348
00:11:34,324 --> 00:11:37,143
the fire was reported again, at the same place,

349
00:11:37,144 --> 00:11:38,303
after numerous callers

350
00:11:38,304 --> 00:11:40,798
to 911 said it was moving fast.

351
00:11:40,858 --> 00:11:42,458
At two minutes to three,

352
00:11:42,518 --> 00:11:45,092
Engine 11 reported it could see smoke.

353
00:11:45,152 --> 00:11:47,951
At three o'clock, Engine 11 arrived and reported

354
00:11:47,952 --> 00:11:49,971
the fire was approximately twenty feet

355
00:11:49,972 --> 00:11:53,451
by a hundred feet, moving rapidly makai —

356
00:11:53,452 --> 00:11:54,634
toward the ocean.

357
00:11:54,694 --> 00:11:57,229
Twenty by a hundred is a fire you can walk

358
00:11:57,289 --> 00:11:57,872
the length of.

359
00:11:57,873 --> 00:11:58,991
At five past three,

360
00:11:58,993 --> 00:12:00,772
police arriving at a shed confirmed

361
00:12:00,773 --> 00:12:02,896
the first structure on fire.

362
00:12:02,956 --> 00:12:03,895
Here is the mechanism,

363
00:12:03,896 --> 00:12:06,958
because everything that follows is this repeated.

364
00:12:07,018 --> 00:12:09,758
Fire moves through a built area three ways:

365
00:12:09,818 --> 00:12:13,063
direct flame contact, radiant heat, and embers.

366
00:12:13,123 --> 00:12:15,602
Embers are made by whatever is burning and carried

367
00:12:15,603 --> 00:12:16,623
by the wind,

368
00:12:16,683 --> 00:12:18,642
and they start new fires beyond the edge

369
00:12:18,643 --> 00:12:19,865
of the old one.

370
00:12:19,925 --> 00:12:21,704
They get into buildings through vents,

371
00:12:21,705 --> 00:12:22,424
through windows,

372
00:12:22,425 --> 00:12:24,824
through openings the wind has already made —

373
00:12:24,825 --> 00:12:27,236
and the building burns from the inside out.

374
00:12:27,237 --> 00:12:28,556
At twenty-one past three,

375
00:12:28,557 --> 00:12:30,816
embers carried by the wind spotted the fire across

376
00:12:30,817 --> 00:12:32,353
the bypass road.

377
00:12:32,413 --> 00:12:34,712
At twenty-three past three, command advised

378
00:12:34,713 --> 00:12:37,433
that the fire had crossed Lahainaluna Road,

379
00:12:37,493 --> 00:12:38,852
that it was in the park,

380
00:12:38,853 --> 00:12:40,492
and that visibility was very poor

381
00:12:40,493 --> 00:12:42,405
because of the amount of smoke.

382
00:12:42,465 --> 00:12:44,165
At twenty-eight past three,

383
00:12:44,225 --> 00:12:45,804
a ladder company reported a structure

384
00:12:45,805 --> 00:12:48,464
on fire south of Lahainaluna Road.

385
00:12:48,524 --> 00:12:49,764
At half past three,

386
00:12:49,824 --> 00:12:51,443
vehicles were burning near the bypass,

387
00:12:51,444 --> 00:12:54,083
and embers were reaching every house west

388
00:12:54,084 --> 00:12:55,776
and south of the park.

389
00:12:55,836 --> 00:12:57,996
At thirty-seven minutes past three,

390
00:12:58,056 --> 00:12:59,838
this went out over the radio.

391
00:12:59,898 --> 00:13:01,517
"There is one house on Lahainaluna

392
00:13:01,518 --> 00:13:03,296
that is fully going now.

393
00:13:03,356 --> 00:13:05,546
We need to stop it where you are.

394
00:13:05,606 --> 00:13:07,726
That has to be the cutoff there,

395
00:13:07,786 --> 00:13:09,422
that road back there."

396
00:13:09,482 --> 00:13:09,961
The engine

397
00:13:09,962 --> 00:13:12,614
that answered said it might be multiple houses.

398
00:13:12,615 --> 00:13:13,594
Command answered:

399
00:13:13,595 --> 00:13:16,025
yeah, there are multiple structures going.

400
00:13:16,026 --> 00:13:18,445
Thirty-seven minutes after the fire was reported,

401
00:13:18,446 --> 00:13:20,645
the question on the radio was no longer where

402
00:13:20,646 --> 00:13:22,025
to put water.

403
00:13:22,085 --> 00:13:24,090
It was where the line was.

404
00:13:24,150 --> 00:13:26,029
At forty-three minutes past three,

405
00:13:26,030 --> 00:13:27,169
an officer reported the smoke

406
00:13:27,170 --> 00:13:29,850
at the highway was getting, in his word,

407
00:13:29,910 --> 00:13:31,031
pretty bad.

408
00:13:31,091 --> 00:13:32,399
Now the warnings.

409
00:13:32,459 --> 00:13:34,158
The county sends emergency messages

410
00:13:34,159 --> 00:13:36,439
the way most American counties do:

411
00:13:36,499 --> 00:13:38,699
as Wireless Emergency Alerts,

412
00:13:38,759 --> 00:13:40,758
the ones that arrive on a phone with a tone

413
00:13:40,759 --> 00:13:43,055
and cannot be switched off.

414
00:13:43,115 --> 00:13:43,994
Its alert log

415
00:13:43,995 --> 00:13:46,194
for that day is in the state's report,

416
00:13:46,195 --> 00:13:47,860
and it begins early.

417
00:13:47,920 --> 00:13:49,739
At nine minutes past four in the morning,

418
00:13:49,740 --> 00:13:53,268
an evacuation order for a subdivision at Kula.

419
00:13:53,328 --> 00:13:56,587
At five o'clock, another one, for a road at Kula.

420
00:13:56,647 --> 00:13:59,859
At twenty-one past five, another, near Makawao.

421
00:13:59,919 --> 00:14:01,538
Those are the upcountry fires,

422
00:14:01,539 --> 00:14:03,138
and they went out in the dark,

423
00:14:03,139 --> 00:14:05,314
hours before the sun came up.

424
00:14:05,374 --> 00:14:08,114
At four minutes past four in the afternoon —

425
00:14:08,174 --> 00:14:09,273
an hour and nine minutes

426
00:14:09,274 --> 00:14:11,854
after the fire was reported at Lahaina —

427
00:14:11,914 --> 00:14:14,856
an evacuation order went out for a subdivision.

428
00:14:14,916 --> 00:14:16,363
It was for Kula.

429
00:14:16,423 --> 00:14:18,042
At eleven minutes past four,

430
00:14:18,043 --> 00:14:19,542
command asked for the power to be cut,

431
00:14:19,543 --> 00:14:22,700
because of the number of poles and wires down.

432
00:14:22,760 --> 00:14:25,427
The dispatcher confirmed it within the minute.

433
00:14:25,428 --> 00:14:28,528
And at sixteen minutes past four in the afternoon,

434
00:14:28,588 --> 00:14:31,187
the first evacuation order in that log that names

435
00:14:31,188 --> 00:14:33,795
a Lahaina neighbourhood was sent.

436
00:14:33,855 --> 00:14:35,628
Kelawea Mauka Subdivision.

437
00:14:35,688 --> 00:14:39,086
Evacuate your family and pets now, do not delay.

438
00:14:39,146 --> 00:14:41,522
Shelter is open at Lahaina Civic Center.

439
00:14:41,582 --> 00:14:42,501
The shelter named

440
00:14:42,502 --> 00:14:44,261
in that message had closed two hours

441
00:14:44,262 --> 00:14:46,187
and sixteen minutes earlier.

442
00:14:46,247 --> 00:14:47,846
And the message was sent to cellphones,

443
00:14:47,847 --> 00:14:50,246
in a region where cellular phone communication

444
00:14:50,247 --> 00:14:52,896
had been destroyed in the late morning.

445
00:14:52,956 --> 00:14:54,635
The County's position is that it sent

446
00:14:54,636 --> 00:14:57,116
at least fourteen alert messages that day,

447
00:14:57,176 --> 00:14:59,795
and that all twenty-one cell towers serving West

448
00:14:59,796 --> 00:15:02,196
Maui, including Lahaina,

449
00:15:02,256 --> 00:15:03,924
experienced total failure.

450
00:15:03,984 --> 00:15:05,543
It sued four carriers over it

451
00:15:05,544 --> 00:15:07,289
in May of twenty twenty-four.

452
00:15:07,349 --> 00:15:09,208
The next entry in that log naming

453
00:15:09,209 --> 00:15:11,568
a Lahaina neighbourhood is at forty-six minutes

454
00:15:11,569 --> 00:15:13,162
past eight that night.

455
00:15:13,222 --> 00:15:15,261
It says to evacuate north, out of town,

456
00:15:15,262 --> 00:15:16,713
toward Kapalua.

457
00:15:16,773 --> 00:15:19,133
At half past four in the afternoon,

458
00:15:19,193 --> 00:15:21,672
the county's emergency operations centre was fully

459
00:15:21,673 --> 00:15:22,818
activated.

460
00:15:22,878 --> 00:15:24,417
It had been at partial activation

461
00:15:24,418 --> 00:15:26,771
since nine o'clock the previous evening,

462
00:15:26,818 --> 00:15:27,997
staffed by two people,

463
00:15:27,998 --> 00:15:30,038
opened for the wind warning.

464
00:15:30,098 --> 00:15:32,357
That agency's full strength was an administrator

465
00:15:32,358 --> 00:15:34,564
and eight direct reports.

466
00:15:34,624 --> 00:15:37,000
Two of them were unavailable that week.

467
00:15:37,060 --> 00:15:39,099
The police department was working normal daily

468
00:15:39,100 --> 00:15:40,179
staffing.

469
00:15:40,239 --> 00:15:41,898
Holding the night shift over on the morning

470
00:15:41,899 --> 00:15:45,541
of the eighth brought the number of officers
in Lahaina town to thirteen.

471
00:15:45,601 --> 00:15:47,188
Thirteen officers.

472
00:15:47,248 --> 00:15:47,947
For a town,

473
00:15:47,948 --> 00:15:49,847
on a day the forecast had been naming it

474
00:15:49,848 --> 00:15:52,796
for five days.

475
00:15:52,856 --> 00:15:54,855
By nightfall the fire had crossed the highway

476
00:15:54,856 --> 00:15:57,554
and burned all the way to the ocean's edge.

477
00:15:57,614 --> 00:15:59,573
When the County of Maui published the origin

478
00:15:59,574 --> 00:16:02,174
and cause of it, fourteen months later,

479
00:16:02,234 --> 00:16:04,313
it recorded that the fire claimed at least

480
00:16:04,314 --> 00:16:06,492
a hundred and two lives.

481
00:16:06,552 --> 00:16:08,231
That is the last number in this film

482
00:16:08,232 --> 00:16:09,764
that is about people.

483
00:16:09,824 --> 00:16:10,303
Everything

484
00:16:10,304 --> 00:16:12,663
after it is about what was already standing

485
00:16:12,664 --> 00:16:15,312
on that slope before the eighth of August.

486
00:16:15,372 --> 00:16:17,111
Because by three in the afternoon

487
00:16:17,112 --> 00:16:19,231
the fire was no longer the only problem,

488
00:16:19,232 --> 00:16:21,417
and it had not been for hours.

489
00:16:21,477 --> 00:16:23,676
The report's summary is that the conflagration

490
00:16:23,677 --> 00:16:26,617
overwhelmed the town's limited evacuation routes,

491
00:16:26,677 --> 00:16:29,216
some of which were blocked by downed utility poles

492
00:16:29,217 --> 00:16:31,051
and electrical lines.

493
00:16:31,111 --> 00:16:33,231
Limited is the operative word,

494
00:16:33,291 --> 00:16:34,930
and the investigators wrote three separate

495
00:16:34,931 --> 00:16:36,367
findings about it.

496
00:16:36,427 --> 00:16:37,686
Severe congestion due

497
00:16:37,687 --> 00:16:39,666
to parked cars along neighbourhood streets

498
00:16:39,667 --> 00:16:42,054
hindered evacuation and response.

499
00:16:42,114 --> 00:16:44,753
Densely populated and narrow roadways hindered

500
00:16:44,754 --> 00:16:46,473
the movement of both the fire department

501
00:16:46,474 --> 00:16:48,066
and the police.

502
00:16:48,126 --> 00:16:50,985
Roadways and evacuation routes were not adequately

503
00:16:50,986 --> 00:16:52,965
maintained before August the eighth

504
00:16:52,966 --> 00:16:55,165
to sustain effective evacuation during

505
00:16:55,166 --> 00:16:56,447
a fire event.

506
00:16:56,507 --> 00:16:57,766
And zoning in some areas

507
00:16:57,767 --> 00:16:59,286
of Lahaina was not commensurate

508
00:16:59,287 --> 00:17:01,266
with the modern built environment,

509
00:17:01,267 --> 00:17:04,270
the environmental risks, or the population growth.

510
00:17:04,330 --> 00:17:06,749
At four minutes past seven that evening, one

511
00:17:06,750 --> 00:17:08,389
of the streets running out of town became

512
00:17:08,390 --> 00:17:09,678
impassable.

513
00:17:09,738 --> 00:17:11,650
Another had already gone.

514
00:17:11,710 --> 00:17:14,086
The report counts what that left.

515
00:17:14,146 --> 00:17:16,085
The potential evacuation exit routes

516
00:17:16,086 --> 00:17:18,764
from Front Street were reduced from eight to six.

517
00:17:18,765 --> 00:17:21,084
At about a quarter to five that afternoon,

518
00:17:21,085 --> 00:17:23,344
an officer working the residential streets found

519
00:17:23,345 --> 00:17:25,805
an access road blocked by a metal gate,

520
00:17:25,865 --> 00:17:27,596
and the gate was locked.

521
00:17:27,656 --> 00:17:29,316
Behind it, by his count,

522
00:17:29,376 --> 00:17:32,308
were thirty to fifty cars that could not get out.

523
00:17:32,368 --> 00:17:34,567
A resident brought a reciprocating saw and cut

524
00:17:34,568 --> 00:17:35,534
the lock.

525
00:17:35,594 --> 00:17:37,633
A chain-link gate nearby was pulled open

526
00:17:37,634 --> 00:17:39,085
with a tow strap.

527
00:17:39,145 --> 00:17:40,639
One side of it opened.

528
00:17:40,699 --> 00:17:41,538
A driver stopped,

529
00:17:41,539 --> 00:17:43,658
because he was not sure there was enough room

530
00:17:43,659 --> 00:17:44,886
to get through.

531
00:17:44,946 --> 00:17:46,765
The officer looked at the buildings next

532
00:17:46,766 --> 00:17:48,045
to the line of cars and saw

533
00:17:48,046 --> 00:17:50,109
that they were now fully engulfed.

534
00:17:50,169 --> 00:17:52,408
So he ran at the gate and put his shoulder

535
00:17:52,409 --> 00:17:54,496
through it to open the other side.

536
00:17:54,556 --> 00:17:56,615
Thirty to fifty fully loaded cars went

537
00:17:56,616 --> 00:17:57,907
through that gate.

538
00:17:57,967 --> 00:17:59,043
One gate.

539
00:17:59,103 --> 00:18:00,318
One officer.

540
00:18:00,378 --> 00:18:03,451
And one saw that a resident happened to own.

541
00:18:03,511 --> 00:18:05,010
The state's investigators turned it

542
00:18:05,011 --> 00:18:06,331
into two findings,

543
00:18:06,391 --> 00:18:09,788
and both of them are about equipment nobody had.

544
00:18:09,848 --> 00:18:12,607
Emergency responders did not have ready capability

545
00:18:12,608 --> 00:18:15,848
to unlock emergency gates at various locations,

546
00:18:15,908 --> 00:18:19,515
including schools, to facilitate evacuations.

547
00:18:19,575 --> 00:18:21,714
They were often forced to rely on a third party

548
00:18:21,715 --> 00:18:23,019
for access.

549
00:18:23,079 --> 00:18:25,338
Police officers encountered barriers on roads

550
00:18:25,339 --> 00:18:26,338
that could have been used

551
00:18:26,339 --> 00:18:27,738
as alternate escape routes,

552
00:18:27,739 --> 00:18:30,657
and lacked the equipment to get through them.

553
00:18:30,717 --> 00:18:33,076
The recommendation asks for police vehicles

554
00:18:33,077 --> 00:18:36,157
to carry kits able to remove chain-link fences,

555
00:18:36,217 --> 00:18:37,784
gates and boulders.

556
00:18:37,844 --> 00:18:38,523
A recommendation

557
00:18:38,524 --> 00:18:40,803
that a police car should carry bolt cutters

558
00:18:40,804 --> 00:18:43,123
is the kind of sentence that only gets written

559
00:18:43,124 --> 00:18:44,446
after something.

560
00:18:44,506 --> 00:18:46,965
Now the water, because the version of this story

561
00:18:46,966 --> 00:18:48,545
that most people carry is wrong,

562
00:18:48,546 --> 00:18:51,387
and the record says so directly.

563
00:18:51,447 --> 00:18:54,026
The common account is that the power failed,

564
00:18:54,027 --> 00:18:56,935
the pumps stopped, and the hydrants went dry.

565
00:18:56,995 --> 00:18:58,094
The twenty-first finding

566
00:18:58,095 --> 00:19:00,874
of the state's investigation is that no pumps

567
00:19:00,875 --> 00:19:03,314
are used outside the water production facilities

568
00:19:03,315 --> 00:19:06,430
to provide pressure in that system at all.

569
00:19:06,490 --> 00:19:09,149
Both systems had uninterrupted electrical power

570
00:19:09,150 --> 00:19:11,729
during the August twenty twenty-three fires,

571
00:19:11,730 --> 00:19:14,894
and produced water at capacity for the duration

572
00:19:14,954 --> 00:19:15,566
of the fire.

573
00:19:15,567 --> 00:19:17,340
Uninterrupted power.

574
00:19:17,400 --> 00:19:18,801
Full capacity.

575
00:19:18,861 --> 00:19:20,216
For the duration.

576
00:19:20,276 --> 00:19:21,215
What actually happened

577
00:19:21,216 --> 00:19:23,295
to the pressure is the twenty-fourth finding,

578
00:19:23,296 --> 00:19:26,135
and it is worse, because nothing failed.

579
00:19:26,195 --> 00:19:27,430
As structures burned,

580
00:19:27,435 --> 00:19:30,155
the household plumbing inside them failed —

581
00:19:30,215 --> 00:19:32,235
plastic and other piping —

582
00:19:32,295 --> 00:19:34,694
allowing unrestricted flow of water from one

583
00:19:34,695 --> 00:19:36,294
or more locations in each home,

584
00:19:36,295 --> 00:19:38,674
so that water flowed freely from more

585
00:19:38,675 --> 00:19:39,494
and more structures,

586
00:19:39,495 --> 00:19:42,968
and the pressure and flow in the fire area fell.

587
00:19:43,028 --> 00:19:45,915
Every house that burned became an open tap.

588
00:19:45,975 --> 00:19:47,574
The system was not losing water

589
00:19:47,575 --> 00:19:49,234
because it was broken.

590
00:19:49,294 --> 00:19:51,293
It was losing water because it was working,

591
00:19:51,294 --> 00:19:53,481
into a thousand holes.

592
00:19:53,541 --> 00:19:55,360
The timeline records what that felt like

593
00:19:55,361 --> 00:19:56,521
on the ground.

594
00:19:56,581 --> 00:19:58,360
Pressure in the mains dropped to the point

595
00:19:58,361 --> 00:20:00,780
that there was no water coming from fire hydrants

596
00:20:00,781 --> 00:20:02,626
in some parts of Lahaina.

597
00:20:02,686 --> 00:20:05,265
A relief engine trying to refill found

598
00:20:05,266 --> 00:20:07,905
a hydrant producing, in the crew's word,

599
00:20:07,906 --> 00:20:08,824
a trickle.

600
00:20:08,884 --> 00:20:10,403
Another crew found good pressure

601
00:20:10,404 --> 00:20:11,984
and filled their tanks —

602
00:20:12,044 --> 00:20:14,691
down at the beach, at the bottom of the hill.

603
00:20:14,710 --> 00:20:16,689
By five past five the next morning,

604
00:20:16,690 --> 00:20:18,209
the hydrants around the civic centre

605
00:20:18,210 --> 00:20:20,430
and the fire station were dry.

606
00:20:20,490 --> 00:20:22,209
And at half past three on the afternoon

607
00:20:22,210 --> 00:20:24,229
of the eighth, the system that tells

608
00:20:24,230 --> 00:20:26,509
the water department how much water it has left

609
00:20:26,510 --> 00:20:27,928
stopped reporting.

610
00:20:27,988 --> 00:20:30,307
No storage tank data was recorded for the rest

611
00:20:30,308 --> 00:20:31,432
of the fire.

612
00:20:31,492 --> 00:20:33,131
Once that connection was lost,

613
00:20:33,132 --> 00:20:35,631
the county's water department did not know how

614
00:20:35,632 --> 00:20:38,514
much stored water was available for firefighting.

615
00:20:38,572 --> 00:20:39,951
The twenty-sixth finding states

616
00:20:39,952 --> 00:20:41,572
the outcome plainly:

617
00:20:41,632 --> 00:20:43,851
water was not provided with sufficient volume

618
00:20:43,852 --> 00:20:46,511
and sufficient pressure for use in firefighting

619
00:20:46,512 --> 00:20:48,379
for the entire fire event.

620
00:20:48,439 --> 00:20:49,778
And the twentieth finding says

621
00:20:49,779 --> 00:20:51,918
the department was seemingly in compliance

622
00:20:51,919 --> 00:20:53,718
with the water system design standards

623
00:20:53,719 --> 00:20:55,877
for the State of Hawaiʻi.

624
00:20:55,937 --> 00:20:57,636
Both of those are true at once,

625
00:20:57,637 --> 00:21:00,403
and the twenty-seventh finding explains why.

626
00:21:00,463 --> 00:21:03,182
Water quality and cost make it impractical to size

627
00:21:03,183 --> 00:21:05,122
a drinking water system to meet

628
00:21:05,123 --> 00:21:08,226
the firefighting demand of an urban conflagration.

629
00:21:08,286 --> 00:21:10,685
A town's water system is built to supply houses

630
00:21:10,686 --> 00:21:12,566
and to fight house fires.

631
00:21:12,626 --> 00:21:15,002
It is not built to fight the town.

632
00:21:15,062 --> 00:21:17,345
The same shape appears at the utility.

633
00:21:17,405 --> 00:21:19,864
The thirtieth finding is that Hawaiian Electric

634
00:21:19,865 --> 00:21:22,204
did not have a Public Safety Power Shut-Off

635
00:21:22,205 --> 00:21:25,145
program in place at the time of the fire —

636
00:21:25,205 --> 00:21:26,964
the procedure, used elsewhere,

637
00:21:26,965 --> 00:21:29,484
of switching lines off in advance

638
00:21:29,485 --> 00:21:31,264
when the weather makes them dangerous.

639
00:21:31,265 --> 00:21:32,664
The twenty-ninth is that a lack

640
00:21:32,665 --> 00:21:34,944
of utility vegetation abatement regulation

641
00:21:34,945 --> 00:21:38,004
and enforcement may have contributed to vegetation

642
00:21:38,005 --> 00:21:39,504
at the base of utility poles

643
00:21:39,505 --> 00:21:41,565
and near transmission lines,

644
00:21:41,625 --> 00:21:43,244
creating a receptive fuel source

645
00:21:43,245 --> 00:21:45,205
for arcing electrical wires.

646
00:21:45,265 --> 00:21:47,224
Receptive fuel source is the language

647
00:21:47,225 --> 00:21:49,081
of an engineering report.

648
00:21:49,141 --> 00:21:51,320
What it describes is dry grass at the bottom

649
00:21:51,321 --> 00:21:52,539
of a pole.

650
00:21:52,599 --> 00:21:54,598
The twenty-eighth is that the utility,

651
00:21:54,599 --> 00:21:57,298
together with the fire and police departments,

652
00:21:57,299 --> 00:21:59,398
did not have an adequate staffing plan

653
00:21:59,399 --> 00:22:02,034
for the wildfire conditions of that day.

654
00:22:02,094 --> 00:22:04,393
And then there is the sixty-first finding,

655
00:22:04,394 --> 00:22:06,885
which is not about equipment at all.

656
00:22:06,945 --> 00:22:08,864
There appears to be a statewide culture

657
00:22:08,865 --> 00:22:12,618
of dismissing and under-recognising wildfire risk.

658
00:22:12,678 --> 00:22:14,357
The underfunding and under-addressing

659
00:22:14,358 --> 00:22:15,857
of preparedness, planning

660
00:22:15,858 --> 00:22:18,637
and mitigation significantly impacts all parts

661
00:22:18,638 --> 00:22:20,999
of the system and fire outcomes.

662
00:22:21,059 --> 00:22:23,098
And then the investigators added a sentence

663
00:22:23,099 --> 00:22:25,723
that appears nowhere else in the eighty-four.

664
00:22:25,724 --> 00:22:29,275
This cannot be overstated.

665
00:22:29,335 --> 00:22:31,075
Three weeks after the fire,

666
00:22:31,135 --> 00:22:33,054
the Attorney General of Hawaiʻi commissioned

667
00:22:33,055 --> 00:22:35,798
an outside investigation of her own state.

668
00:22:35,858 --> 00:22:38,798
She engaged the Fire Safety Research Institute,

669
00:22:38,858 --> 00:22:40,978
part of UL Research Institutes,

670
00:22:41,038 --> 00:22:43,078
to conduct a comprehensive,

671
00:22:43,138 --> 00:22:45,877
independent analysis assessing the policies

672
00:22:45,878 --> 00:22:47,877
and performance of state and county agencies

673
00:22:47,878 --> 00:22:50,237
in preparing for and responding

674
00:22:50,238 --> 00:22:52,027
to the Maui wildfires.

675
00:22:52,087 --> 00:22:53,907
Her own words at the time:

676
00:22:53,967 --> 00:22:56,767
"I am committed to an independent, unbiased,

677
00:22:56,827 --> 00:22:58,186
and transparent investigation

678
00:22:58,187 --> 00:23:01,197
into the government actions during the fires."

679
00:23:01,257 --> 00:23:02,716
The first report came in April

680
00:23:02,717 --> 00:23:04,237
of twenty twenty-four.

681
00:23:04,297 --> 00:23:07,476
Three hundred and seventy-five pages,

682
00:23:07,477 --> 00:23:09,676
and a minute-by-minute timeline built from more

683
00:23:09,677 --> 00:23:11,576
than twelve thousand records,

684
00:23:11,577 --> 00:23:15,231
covering the afternoon of the eighth
through half past eight the next morning.

685
00:23:15,232 --> 00:23:16,131
It says of itself

686
00:23:16,132 --> 00:23:18,630
that it does not analyse causation.

687
00:23:18,690 --> 00:23:21,484
It only establishes what happened, and when.

688
00:23:21,544 --> 00:23:23,317
The second came in September.

689
00:23:23,377 --> 00:23:25,846
Five hundred and eighteen pages.

690
00:23:25,906 --> 00:23:29,246
Eighty-four findings and a hundred

691
00:23:29,306 --> 00:23:33,065
and forty recommendations,
drawn from an eight hundred

692
00:23:33,066 --> 00:23:37,526
and fifty gigabyte evidence database

693
00:23:37,586 --> 00:23:39,164
of body-camera footage, dispatch audio,

694
00:23:39,165 --> 00:23:39,313
vehicle location data,

695
00:23:39,314 --> 00:23:39,812
interviews and official documents.

696
00:23:39,813 --> 00:23:41,712
Two of those eighty-four findings are the reason

697
00:23:41,713 --> 00:23:43,211
this film exists.

698
00:23:43,271 --> 00:23:44,904
Finding thirty-seven.

699
00:23:44,964 --> 00:23:45,983
Only one siren

700
00:23:45,984 --> 00:23:48,263
from the All-Hazard Outdoor Warning Siren System

701
00:23:48,264 --> 00:23:50,023
was operable within the burn perimeter

702
00:23:50,024 --> 00:23:53,572
of the Lahaina area on August the eighth,

703
00:23:53,632 --> 00:23:55,071
twenty twenty-three.
One.

704
00:23:55,131 --> 00:23:57,136
Inside the area that burned.

705
00:23:57,196 --> 00:23:59,235
Reporting at the time put the number of sirens

706
00:23:59,236 --> 00:24:00,695
in the Lahaina area at four,

707
00:24:00,696 --> 00:24:03,515
and described all four of them as sited along

708
00:24:03,516 --> 00:24:04,588
the shore.

709
00:24:04,648 --> 00:24:06,927
Finding thirty-eight is a separate finding,

710
00:24:06,928 --> 00:24:08,464
about a separate thing.

711
00:24:08,524 --> 00:24:10,863
The All-Hazard Outdoor Warning Siren System

712
00:24:10,864 --> 00:24:12,623
had not been utilised for warning

713
00:24:12,624 --> 00:24:15,263
of wildland-urban interface fires prior to August

714
00:24:15,264 --> 00:24:17,541
the eighth, twenty twenty-three.

715
00:24:17,601 --> 00:24:18,956
Not that day.

716
00:24:19,016 --> 00:24:20,045
Ever.

717
00:24:20,105 --> 00:24:20,924
In the whole life

718
00:24:20,925 --> 00:24:22,724
of the largest outdoor warning network

719
00:24:22,725 --> 00:24:23,525
in the world,

720
00:24:23,585 --> 00:24:25,144
it had never once been used to warn

721
00:24:25,145 --> 00:24:26,289
of a fire.

722
00:24:26,349 --> 00:24:27,988
And it was not used on the eighth

723
00:24:27,989 --> 00:24:29,236
of August either.

724
00:24:29,296 --> 00:24:31,095
Reporting at the time established that,

725
00:24:31,096 --> 00:24:31,575
and the head

726
00:24:31,576 --> 00:24:33,675
of the county's emergency management agency

727
00:24:33,676 --> 00:24:36,456
confirmed it publicly within days.

728
00:24:36,516 --> 00:24:38,835
At a news conference on the sixteenth of August,

729
00:24:38,836 --> 00:24:41,895
twenty twenty-three, he was asked

730
00:24:41,896 --> 00:24:45,276
whether he regretted not activating them.
His answer was three words.

731
00:24:45,336 --> 00:24:46,551
I do not.

732
00:24:46,611 --> 00:24:48,384
And he gave his reason.

733
00:24:48,444 --> 00:24:50,143
Had we sounded the sirens that night,

734
00:24:50,144 --> 00:24:52,083
we were afraid that people would have gone mauka —

735
00:24:52,084 --> 00:24:54,164
toward the mountainside —

736
00:24:54,224 --> 00:24:55,683
and if that was the case,

737
00:24:55,684 --> 00:24:57,474
they would have gone into the fire.

738
00:24:57,475 --> 00:24:58,794
He resigned the next day,

739
00:24:58,795 --> 00:25:02,080
the seventeenth of August, citing health reasons.

740
00:25:02,140 --> 00:25:04,609
He has not been charged with any offence.

741
00:25:04,669 --> 00:25:06,228
The last recommendation attached

742
00:25:06,229 --> 00:25:07,788
to Finding thirty-seven asks

743
00:25:07,789 --> 00:25:09,768
for a statewide sustainable programme

744
00:25:09,769 --> 00:25:12,189
for the outdoor warning system,

745
00:25:12,249 --> 00:25:14,308
including functioning hardware resilient

746
00:25:14,309 --> 00:25:17,262
against mass communications failure.

747
00:25:17,322 --> 00:25:20,395
Resilient against mass communications failure.

748
00:25:20,455 --> 00:25:22,274
That phrase is in the recommendation

749
00:25:22,275 --> 00:25:25,385
because of what the alternative turned out to be.

750
00:25:25,445 --> 00:25:26,704
The findings about the alerts

751
00:25:26,705 --> 00:25:28,936
that were sent are just as flat.

752
00:25:28,996 --> 00:25:30,536
Finding thirty-six.

753
00:25:30,596 --> 00:25:32,815
Many residents did not receive a text notification

754
00:25:32,816 --> 00:25:34,575
from the county regarding the high winds

755
00:25:34,576 --> 00:25:36,177
and high fire danger.

756
00:25:36,237 --> 00:25:38,149
Finding seventy-five.

757
00:25:38,209 --> 00:25:39,088
The alert systems

758
00:25:39,089 --> 00:25:41,488
in place did not adequately inform residents

759
00:25:41,489 --> 00:25:43,139
of inherent dangers.

760
00:25:43,199 --> 00:25:44,638
Its first recommendation asks

761
00:25:44,639 --> 00:25:46,779
for multiple alert systems —

762
00:25:46,839 --> 00:25:48,639
sirens, radio broadcasts,

763
00:25:48,699 --> 00:25:50,581
and door-to-door notifications —

764
00:25:50,639 --> 00:25:51,978
especially when cell service

765
00:25:51,979 --> 00:25:54,259
and electrical power are lost.

766
00:25:54,319 --> 00:25:55,581
Door-to-door.

767
00:25:55,641 --> 00:25:57,840
That is the fallback the recommendation reaches

768
00:25:57,841 --> 00:26:01,161
for, and on the night itself it is what happened:

769
00:26:01,221 --> 00:26:03,120
an engine crew driving Wahikuli

770
00:26:03,121 --> 00:26:05,541
at twenty-four minutes past eleven,

771
00:26:05,601 --> 00:26:08,652
running its vehicle sirens and knocking on doors.

772
00:26:08,712 --> 00:26:10,871
And Finding thirty-nine is the one that is hardest

773
00:26:10,872 --> 00:26:12,017
to read.

774
00:26:12,077 --> 00:26:14,717
Even when people were told to evacuate,

775
00:26:14,777 --> 00:26:16,136
and conditions seemed obvious

776
00:26:16,137 --> 00:26:19,336
that evacuation was necessary, many refused,

777
00:26:19,337 --> 00:26:20,936
because there did not appear

778
00:26:20,937 --> 00:26:22,416
to be official notification

779
00:26:22,417 --> 00:26:24,531
that danger was imminent.

780
00:26:24,591 --> 00:26:26,331
People were standing in it,

781
00:26:26,391 --> 00:26:27,690
being told by other people to go,

782
00:26:27,691 --> 00:26:29,190
and waiting for the thing

783
00:26:29,191 --> 00:26:31,054
that says it is official.

784
00:26:31,114 --> 00:26:32,953
There is one more thing in the first report,

785
00:26:32,954 --> 00:26:35,626
and it is four sentences long.

786
00:26:35,686 --> 00:26:37,045
There is no data showing

787
00:26:37,046 --> 00:26:39,245
which emergency management personnel responded

788
00:26:39,246 --> 00:26:40,709
on August the eighth.

789
00:26:40,769 --> 00:26:42,308
The only missing sign-in sheet

790
00:26:42,309 --> 00:26:44,008
for the emergency operations centre

791
00:26:44,009 --> 00:26:46,953
is that agency's sheet, for that day.

792
00:26:47,013 --> 00:26:48,492
The county has not produced it

793
00:26:48,493 --> 00:26:50,318
after multiple requests.

794
00:26:50,378 --> 00:26:52,257
The activity logs that would record

795
00:26:52,258 --> 00:26:54,757
the response hour by hour were not received

796
00:26:54,758 --> 00:26:55,957
from that agency's personnel

797
00:26:55,958 --> 00:26:57,538
for those dates either.

798
00:26:57,598 --> 00:27:00,478
And so the report says, in its own words,

799
00:27:00,538 --> 00:27:02,977
that because of missing data it is difficult

800
00:27:02,978 --> 00:27:05,017
to make a complete and accurate accounting

801
00:27:05,018 --> 00:27:06,437
of activities within

802
00:27:06,438 --> 00:27:08,957
the emergency operations centre from August

803
00:27:08,958 --> 00:27:11,352
the seventh through August the ninth.

804
00:27:11,412 --> 00:27:13,191
The investigators had subpoena power,

805
00:27:13,192 --> 00:27:14,717
and they used it.

806
00:27:14,777 --> 00:27:15,917
One subpoena,

807
00:27:15,977 --> 00:27:18,276
served on the county's emergency management agency

808
00:27:18,277 --> 00:27:20,796
in October of twenty twenty-three,

809
00:27:20,797 --> 00:27:23,076
asked for all maintenance and testing logs

810
00:27:23,077 --> 00:27:25,356
for the statewide alert and warning siren system

811
00:27:25,357 --> 00:27:26,488
in Maui County.

812
00:27:26,548 --> 00:27:28,785
They had to ask for those in writing.

813
00:27:28,845 --> 00:27:30,444
The civil case has moved further

814
00:27:30,445 --> 00:27:31,964
than anything else.

815
00:27:32,024 --> 00:27:33,184
A four billion,

816
00:27:33,244 --> 00:27:35,723
thirty-seven million dollar settlement resolving

817
00:27:35,724 --> 00:27:37,423
roughly four hundred

818
00:27:37,424 --> 00:27:39,212
and fifty lawsuits was announced in August

819
00:27:39,213 --> 00:27:41,900
of twenty twenty-four.
In February of twenty twenty-six,

820
00:27:41,901 --> 00:27:44,900
the Hawaiʻi Supreme Court ruled unanimously

821
00:27:44,901 --> 00:27:47,112
that insurers could not intervene in it.

822
00:27:47,113 --> 00:27:49,192
The first award determination notices went

823
00:27:49,193 --> 00:27:52,415
out on the seventeenth of June, twenty twenty-six.

824
00:27:52,475 --> 00:27:54,991
A notice is an offer, not a payment.

825
00:27:55,051 --> 00:27:57,330
Nearly twenty-two thousand claimants have filed

826
00:27:57,331 --> 00:27:59,656
more than ninety-four thousand claims.

827
00:27:59,716 --> 00:28:01,235
As of August twenty twenty-six,

828
00:28:01,236 --> 00:28:02,707
no payment has been made.

829
00:28:02,710 --> 00:28:04,549
An appeal over how much of the settlement

830
00:28:04,550 --> 00:28:05,969
the lawyers receive is pending

831
00:28:05,970 --> 00:28:08,150
before the state Supreme Court,

832
00:28:08,210 --> 00:28:09,609
and while it is pending,

833
00:28:09,610 --> 00:28:11,727
no settlement payment can be made.

834
00:28:11,787 --> 00:28:14,726
About one point one billion dollars is sitting

835
00:28:14,727 --> 00:28:18,496
in trust for the first of four annual instalments.

836
00:28:18,556 --> 00:28:20,607
So here is what the record holds.

837
00:28:20,667 --> 00:28:23,406
A forecast that was right, five days early,

838
00:28:23,407 --> 00:28:25,087
and named the town.

839
00:28:25,147 --> 00:28:28,127
A warning that looked like
an ordinary summer Tuesday.

840
00:28:28,187 --> 00:28:31,213
Weather data from an airport on another island.

841
00:28:31,273 --> 00:28:33,392
Broken lines re-energised over grass

842
00:28:33,393 --> 00:28:34,996
that had not been cut.

843
00:28:35,056 --> 00:28:38,082
Poles across the northbound lanes before dawn.

844
00:28:38,142 --> 00:28:40,421
A fire put out by the method that works,

845
00:28:40,422 --> 00:28:43,769
in weather the method was not built for.

846
00:28:43,829 --> 00:28:45,694
Phones gone by late morning.

847
00:28:45,754 --> 00:28:49,074
An evacuation order at sixteen minutes past four,

848
00:28:49,134 --> 00:28:51,594
naming a shelter that had closed at two,

849
00:28:51,654 --> 00:28:54,214
sent to a network that had already died.

850
00:28:54,274 --> 00:28:56,279
Eight ways out reduced to six.

851
00:28:56,339 --> 00:28:57,972
A padlocked gate.

852
00:28:58,032 --> 00:29:00,152
A water system in compliance,

853
00:29:00,212 --> 00:29:02,929
bleeding out through a thousand burning houses.

854
00:29:02,930 --> 00:29:05,249
One siren operable inside the burn perimeter,

855
00:29:05,250 --> 00:29:07,509
on a network that had never once been used

856
00:29:07,510 --> 00:29:08,743
for a fire.

857
00:29:08,803 --> 00:29:10,483
Eighty-four findings.

858
00:29:10,543 --> 00:29:12,966
A hundred and forty recommendations.

859
00:29:13,026 --> 00:29:15,025
And not one of them says that sounding

860
00:29:15,026 --> 00:29:17,538
the siren would have changed the outcome.

861
00:29:17,598 --> 00:29:19,371
That is not a loose end.

862
00:29:19,431 --> 00:29:21,111
That is the finding.

863
00:29:21,171 --> 00:29:24,271
The report's own conclusion is a system —

864
00:29:24,331 --> 00:29:28,551
weather, fuel, building codes, roads, water,

865
00:29:28,611 --> 00:29:30,111
power and warning —

866
00:29:30,171 --> 00:29:32,090
and a system is exactly what nobody

867
00:29:32,091 --> 00:29:34,043
can be prosecuted for.

868
00:29:34,103 --> 00:29:36,462
And there are things this film cannot tell you,

869
00:29:36,463 --> 00:29:39,405
because they are not in what has been published.

870
00:29:39,465 --> 00:29:41,284
How much of the town burned in acres,

871
00:29:41,285 --> 00:29:43,444
and how fast the wind was actually blowing

872
00:29:43,445 --> 00:29:46,364
on that slope, are not in the record we read,

873
00:29:46,365 --> 00:29:48,993
and we have not put a number on them.

874
00:29:49,053 --> 00:29:51,569
Here is the part that is not about Maui.

875
00:29:51,629 --> 00:29:53,708
Every place you have ever lived has a warning

876
00:29:53,709 --> 00:29:54,841
system.

877
00:29:54,901 --> 00:29:57,621
And every warning system is really a habit —

878
00:29:57,681 --> 00:30:00,320
the one thing it gets used for, over and over,

879
00:30:00,321 --> 00:30:01,620
until that becomes

880
00:30:01,621 --> 00:30:04,336
the only thing anybody believes it means.

881
00:30:04,396 --> 00:30:06,540
In Hawaiʻi the habit was the sea.

882
00:30:06,600 --> 00:30:08,326
The equipment was general.

883
00:30:08,386 --> 00:30:10,994
Its own published list included wildfires.

884
00:30:11,054 --> 00:30:13,153
But the habit had one direction in it,

885
00:30:13,154 --> 00:30:15,034
and the direction was makai,

886
00:30:15,094 --> 00:30:16,913
and on the eighth of August the fire came

887
00:30:16,914 --> 00:30:18,353
from the other side.

888
00:30:18,413 --> 00:30:19,675
That has changed.

889
00:30:19,735 --> 00:30:22,395
As of the publication of the second report,

890
00:30:22,455 --> 00:30:24,294
the county has implemented a process

891
00:30:24,295 --> 00:30:27,405
for activating the sirens for wildfires.

892
00:30:27,465 --> 00:30:28,464
So this is the ask,

893
00:30:28,465 --> 00:30:30,399
and it is not the usual one.

894
00:30:30,459 --> 00:30:31,058
Find out what

895
00:30:31,059 --> 00:30:33,452
the warning where you live is actually for.

896
00:30:33,453 --> 00:30:35,593
Not what you assume it means —

897
00:30:35,653 --> 00:30:37,592
what the agency that owns it has published

898
00:30:37,593 --> 00:30:38,813
that it means,

899
00:30:38,873 --> 00:30:40,632
and what you are supposed to do in the minute

900
00:30:40,633 --> 00:30:42,006
after you hear it.

901
00:30:42,066 --> 00:30:43,905
In Hawaiʻi the answer is one line long,

902
00:30:43,906 --> 00:30:45,785
and it has been on a public page

903
00:30:45,786 --> 00:30:47,229
the whole time.

904
00:30:47,289 --> 00:30:48,748
When you hear a siren tone

905
00:30:48,749 --> 00:30:52,127
that is not a scheduled test, turn on the radio.

906
00:30:52,187 --> 00:30:54,470
The sound was never the message.

907
00:30:54,530 --> 00:30:57,601
It was the instruction to go and find one.
